window.docContents[19].resolve({"/rules/PL1005/#PL1005-fix":{"contents":"1. Find the axiom that raises the label in the diagnostic's axiom list, then find the lemma or tactic that introduces it (for example simp lemmas using propext, or classical reasoning using Classical.choice).2. Prove the statement constructively or with a narrower lemma so the exact set fits the claim.3. If the stronger foundation is intended, change the surface's claim and rationale explicitly; this changes the published claim and needs review.\n\n","context":"Plumb for Lean rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009PL1005: Transitive axioms must fit the selected profile","header":"How to fix it","id":"/rules/PL1005/#PL1005-fix"},"/rules/PL2004/#PL2004-fix":{"contents":"1. Delete imports of excluded modules (for example checker or fixture modules) from claimed code.2. Use a glob with the intended meaning, such as .andSubmodules `Lib in lakefile.lean or [\"Lib\", \"Lib.+\"] in lakefile.toml, so every intended module is in the library.3. Classify any new root library or executable in the manifest (PL2002).\n\n","context":"Plumb for Lean rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009PL2004: Owned coverage must match the exact Lake inventory","header":"How to fix it","id":"/rules/PL2004/#PL2004-fix"},"/rules/PL4002/#PL4002-fix":{"contents":"1. Fix the underlying finding shown with this diagnostic (for example prove the statement instead of declaring an axiom).2. If the example is meant to fail, mark it with an exact lean-fail marker instead (PL4003).3. Import what the example needs inside the fence; the checker inserts nothing.\n\n","context":"Plumb for Lean rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009PL4002: Positive examples require warning-free elaboration and admission","header":"How to fix it","id":"/rules/PL4002/#PL4002-fix"},"/rules/PL5001/#PL5001-fix":{"contents":"1. Add /-! … -/ at the top of the module, after the imports.2. Follow the template in standard §5.3: purpose, main declarations with their results and hypotheses, assumptions and dependencies, design notes. Keep only sections that help.\n\n","context":"Plumb for Lean rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009PL5001: Claimed modules require module documentation","header":"How to fix it","id":"/rules/PL5001/#PL5001-fix"}});